    "title": "City of DeFuniak Springs moves to bi-monthly Code Enforcement Hearings - NewsBreak",
    "text": "DEFUNIAK SPRINGS, Fla. (WMBB) – The City of Defuniak Springs is adjusting its Code Enforcement Special Magistrate hearing schedule in 2026 from monthly to bi-monthly instead. They say the change is designed to be more cost-effective for taxpayers while giving property owners additional benefits. Starting in January 2026, hearings will take place on the third Thursday of the scheduled months: January, March, May, July, and September. In addition, a special hearing will be held in October. The city says they specifically avoid scheduling hearings in November and December to reduce unnecessary stress for residents during the holidays. “Adjusting to a bi-monthly schedule allows us to manage cost responsibly while also giving our citizens more time to bring properties into compliance. We believe this change strikes the right balance for both the city and our community members,” said Christopher Strawn, City of Defuniak Springs Code Enforcement. “ For more information, contact the community development department at 850-892-8500 ext. 1116 or visit www.defuniaksprings.net . For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to mypanhandle.com.",
